    <!-- 3. Academic Eligibility -->
    <div class="ec-card blue-left">
        <div class="ec-card-title"><span>🎓</span> Academic Eligibility Criteria (Undergraduate &amp; Lateral Entry)</div>
        <h4>A. BS Four-Year Programs (First Semester Entry):</h4>
        <ul>
            <li>The candidates from Sindh province, who have passed Intermediate (HSC-II) or equivalent examination from 2019 to 2022, from any Board of Intermediate &amp; Secondary Education can apply for the admissions.</li>
            <li>Candidates from other provinces can also apply on the reserved seats only.</li>
            <li>Anyone who has passed the H.S.C Part-II Intermediate Examination or any other examination recognized as equivalent annual/Supplementary 2017 to 2021 and annual 2022 is eligible with minimum of 50% marks for Arts/Commerce Students.</li>
            <li>A candidate who has passed H.S.C Part-II Commerce Examination is also eligible for admission to BS program except Natural and Physical Science faculties.</li>
            <li>A candidate who has already completed Bachelor's pass Degree is not eligible for admission to BS course in any discipline.</li>
            <li>A candidate having completed their regular scheme of study in BS/M.A/M.Com/MPA/MBA or any other 16 Year regular programs shall not be eligible for admission in 16 years program.</li>
        </ul>
        <h4>B. Lateral Entry to BS Part-III (Fifth Semester):</h4>
        <ul>
            <li>Anyone who has passed the Bachelor's / Associate Degree examinations from this or any other recognized University shall be eligible to seek admission to BS Part-III provided that he/she fulfills the requirement of minimum marks and other conditions.</li>
            <li>A candidate who has passed 2 years Bachelor / ADE examination earliest in 2017 with a minimum of 50% marks shall be eligible for admission in BS Part-III and will be awarded the BS (4 Years) Degree on completion.</li>
        </ul>
        <h4>C. Special Professional &amp; Departmental Criteria:</h4>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Department of Pharmacy:</strong> For admission in Department of Pharmacy, the candidate should have obtained minimum 60% marks (B Grade) in Intermediate/HSC- (Biology group).</li>
            <li><strong>Faculty of Law:</strong> For Candidates Applying in Law, it is mandatory to have LAT Score of minimum 50%.</li>
            <li>
                <strong>Master's Programs (Previous):</strong>
                <ul>
                    <li>A candidate who has passed B.Sc. Annual/Semester examination 2018 to 2022 with a minimum of 50% marks shall be eligible for seeking admission to M.Sc. (Previous).</li>
                    <li>A candidate who has passed B.Sc./B.A/ B.Com (Pass) examination with minimum of 50% marks shall be eligible for seeking admission to M.A/M.Com/MPA (Previous).</li>
                    <li>A candidate who has passed B.Com (Pass) examination with a minimum of 50% marks shall be eligible for seeking admission to M.Com (Previous).</li>
                </ul>
            </li>
        </ul>
    </div>

    <!-- 4. Nationality -->
    <div class="ec-card green-left">
        <div class="ec-card-title"><span>🇵🇰</span> Nationality &amp; Admission Authority</div>
        <ul>
            <li>A candidate who desires to take admission in the University be a national of Pakistan. The foreigners may be considered for admission only when nominated/recommended by the Ministry of Education, Ministry of Finance &amp; Economic Affairs Division, Government of Pakistan.</li>
            <li>All the admissions shall be provisional until approved by the Vice Chancellor.</li>
            <li>Vice Chancellor may refuse admission to any candidate without mentioning any reason.</li>
        </ul>
    </div>

    <!-- 5. Code of Conduct -->
    <div class="ec-card purple-left">
        <div class="ec-card-title"><span>⚖️</span> University Rules, Student Code of Conduct &amp; Discipline</div>
        <ul>
            <li>A student of the University admitted to any discipline as a regular student shall not appear in any examination as an external candidate during his/her University studentship.</li>
            <li>No change of department shall be allowed once the admission is taken.</li>
            <li>A student shall do all the necessary written work, tutorial and seminars as directed by his/her teachers to his/her satisfaction.</li>
            <li>A student shall do nothing, either in or outside the University that may interfere with the orderly administration and discipline or may bring the University and its administration into disrepute.</li>
            <li>The admission of student shall stand cancelled automatically if he/she occupies the University hostel or any other part forcibly or illegally.</li>
            <li>The University authorities shall not be responsible for providing transport facility to the students as transportation charges are not included in the fees.</li>
            <li>Any student who is enrolled in the evening program will not be allowed to transfer to the morning program.</li>
            <li>The regular student is required to maintain at least <strong>75% of attendance</strong> as eligibility to appear in the examination.</li>
            <li>No student shall be re-admitted without the prior permission of the Vice Chancellor, in case his/her admission is cancelled due to any reason.</li>
            <li>No ex-student shall be given access to the facilities of using the library, laboratories, seminars, etc. without the prior permission of the Vice Chancellor.</li>
        </ul>
    </div>

    <!-- 6. ID Card -->
    <div class="ec-card amber-left">
        <div class="ec-card-title"><span>🪪</span> Student Identity Card Regulations</div>
        <ul>
            <li>Each student admitted to a four-year program or post-graduate class shall obtain identity card on the prescribed form on payment of the prescribed fee.</li>
            <li>In case where identity card is lost or destroyed, a duplicate must be obtained immediately at the payment of <strong>Rs. 300/=</strong>.</li>
        </ul>
